  "interpretation": "Parenthesized tail macros are expressions and do not create anonymous block modules. Brace/semicolon statement macros and unrelated items do; even a macro expanding to no nodes retains that boundary. Trait discovery visits the initial module, then hygienic parents, and can see both caller and definition imports. Method names and trait binding names have separate contexts.",
